# Line endings are decided here, not by each clone's core.autocrlf.
#
# Why this file exists: most of this repo's generated code is written by tools
# running in Linux containers -- `sqlc generate`, golangci-lint, the pre-push
# checks -- and they emit LF. A Windows checkout with core.autocrlf=true writes
# CRLF instead, so every `sqlc generate` left ~29 files that `git status`
# reported as modified while `git diff` showed nothing at all: the content was
# identical once normalized, only the bytes on disk differed. That noise buried
# real changes and had to be cleaned up by hand each time (it is also why
# .githooks/pre-push strips CR before running gofmt).
#
# The index has always stored LF, so pinning eol=lf changes no blob -- it only
# makes the working tree match what those tools already produce.

* text=auto eol=lf

# cmd.exe requires CRLF: a batch file with LF line endings fails in ways that
# are hard to read. The Gradle wrapper ships one (android/gradlew.bat).
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf

# Binary: never normalized, never diffed as text. Git already detects these by
# content; listing them makes the intent explicit and skips the sniffing.
*.png binary
*.ico binary
*.jar binary
